<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Runs `guildhall --headless` at login: serves the browser view and draws
  nothing, so your phone and your other machines can reach it whether or not the
  room is open in a terminal.

  Edit the two paths below to match this machine, then:
    cp contrib/dev.guildhall.headless.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/dev.guildhall.headless.plist

  To stop it, or to stop it starting at login:
    launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/dev.guildhall.headless.plist

  It is running when this answers:
    curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' http://127.0.0.1:4318/    # 401 = up

  A 401 is the passcode gate, which means the server is answering. Anything else
  — no connection at all — means it is not.

  **`node` by absolute path, not `guildhall`.** launchd starts with almost no
  environment and no shell profile, so nvm's PATH does not exist and the linked
  `guildhall` command is not found. `which node` from your shell prints the path
  to put here; on nvm it looks like
  /Users/you/.nvm/versions/node/v22.0.0/bin/node.

  **Not both this and the guard.** `--headless` already holds sleep off while
  sessions work, so running dev.guildhall.guard alongside it means two processes
  polling the same registry and asserting the same thing. Pick one; this one if
  you want the browser view.

  **The port comes from ~/.config/guildhall/config.json.** Add `--port 4400`
  after `--headless` below to override it for this service only, which is what
  you want if something else on the machine already holds 4318 — guildhall does
  not pick another port for you, it reports the clash and gives up.

  KeepAlive restarts it if it dies. That matters more here than for the guard: a
  status page that quietly stopped answering looks, from a phone, exactly like a
  machine that is asleep.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>Label</key>
	<string>dev.guildhall.headless</string>

	<key>ProgramArguments</key>
	<array>
		<string>/Users/CHANGEME/.nvm/versions/node/v22.0.0/bin/node</string>
		<string>/Users/CHANGEME/projects/guildhall/dist/main.mjs</string>
		<string>--headless</string>
	</array>

	<key>RunAtLoad</key>
	<true/>
	<key>KeepAlive</key>
	<true/>

	<key>StandardOutPath</key>
	<string>/tmp/guildhall-headless.log</string>
	<key>StandardErrorPath</key>
	<string>/tmp/guildhall-headless.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
